// Port of compiler/src/i18n/ (i18n.c, i18n.h, i18n_internal.h + the data
// tables of i18n_gettext.c). Flat single-file module
// (see salam/PORTING.md "Layout - FLAT"): i18n_gettext.c + i18n_load.c +
// i18n_locale.c merged below, with `// ===== <file>.c =====` markers.
//
// This file carries the package's globals and every private helper so the
// file satisfies E083/E085/E088 (the pub API follows the helpers).
//
// C -> Salam decisions for this module:
// - k_msgs[] ({en, fa, ar} rows, i18n_gettext.c) -> three parallel str
//   arrays k_msg_en/k_msg_fa/k_msg_ar, generated mechanically from the C
//   source so every string is byte-for-byte identical. Lookup is the same
//   linear scan over the English column (first match wins).
// - i18n_msg_t / i18n_pair_t structs -> parallel arrays (no struct needed).
// - g_dyn_words / g_dyn_vals fixed C arrays (+counters) -> Vector<str>
//   triples (lang/alias/canon); the C capacity caps (I18N_DYN_MAX = 512,
//   I18N_DYN_VAL_MAX = 256) are still enforced, and like the C arrays the
//   registries live for the whole process (never freed).
// - k_layout_fa / k_value_fa static fallback tables are EMPTY in the C
//   source ({{NULL, NULL}}), so the fa fallback scans are not ported (they
//   can never match); LayoutWord/LayoutValue go straight to the fallback.
// - const char* NULL guards are dropped (Salam str is never null).
// - i18n_active_lang() (i18n_internal.h) is not exported: inside the merged
//   package siblings read g_i18n_lang directly; external consumers use Lang().
// - byte-wise loose comparison (i18n_words_equal_loose) is re-expressed
//   over UTF-8 codepoints via str.Chars - equivalent for valid UTF-8:
//   both sides are compared after skipping spaces and ZWNJ (U+200C).
package i18n

import str

// I18N_DYN_MAX / I18N_DYN_VAL_MAX (i18n_load.c)
const I18N_DYN_MAX := 512
const I18N_DYN_VAL_MAX := 256

// g_i18n_lang (i18n_locale.c)
mut g_i18n_lang := "en"

// g_dyn_words[] + g_dyn_words_n (i18n_load.c) - parallel columns
mut g_dyn_word_lang := Vector {} as Vector<str>
mut g_dyn_word_alias := Vector {} as Vector<str>
mut g_dyn_word_canon := Vector {} as Vector<str>

// g_dyn_vals[] + g_dyn_vals_n (i18n_load.c) - parallel columns
mut g_dyn_val_lang := Vector {} as Vector<str>
mut g_dyn_val_alias := Vector {} as Vector<str>
mut g_dyn_val_canon := Vector {} as Vector<str>

// ZWNJ (U+200C), the byte sequence i18n_zwnj_at() tests for
k_i18n_zwnj := "\xE2\x80\x8C"

